{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For all flesh had corrupted its way</b> — What our ancient ancestors of blessed memory said, that the sense of “had corrupted its way” is that every living creature did not guard its way of reproduction and deviated from the established, known path, is correct. And how precious is the interpretation they interpreted: that they corrupted with water, and HaShem punished them with water, and just as their waters were from above and below, so were the waters with which He destroyed them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:29.656413564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}